# Certification exams: the questions, options and messages of the Steam and LV exams.
# A backslash followed by n is a line break.
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.introduction=Welcome to the GregTech Electrical Safety Board.\n\nBefore leaving the Steam Age, you must prove that you can tell a power cable from a very expensive fuse. Previous player didn't finish their application and is now spread across three chunks.\n\nAnswer at least 8 of the following 10 questions correctly. Reading tooltips is mandatory, replacing tooltips with guessing is not.
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.passed=Congratulations! You are now a Certified GregTech Electrician.\n\nYou may leave the Steam Age and begin making expensive mistakes with cables. Your certificate confirms that you knew better. It does not cover replacement machines.
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.failed=Certification denied.\n\nPlease return to the Steam Age. The boiler would like a word with you, but at least it cannot send you an MV packet.
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q01.prompt=What is the maximum voltage of the LV tier?
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q01.a=8 V
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q01.b=32 V
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q01.c=128 V
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q01.d=Whatever the cable believes in
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q02.prompt=What is the maximum voltage of the MV tier?
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q02.a=33 V because it is slightly more medium
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q02.b=64 V
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q02.c=128 V
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q02.d=Enough to turn an LV machine into a memory
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q03.prompt=Four LV generators supply the same cable. Does their voltage add up to MV?
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q03.a=No. They can supply more amperage at LV voltage, and you're going to do that a lot here anyway
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q03.b=Yes. Four small numbers always become bigger number
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q03.c=Only if the generators face each other and agree
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q03.d=No, for that you'd need to craft the generators into a 2×2 square first
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q04.prompt=An LV machine receives a 128 V packet through an MV-rated cable. What happens?
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q04.a=It becomes an MV machine for free
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q04.b=It politely rejects the packet and sends you a warning letter within 7 business days
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q04.c=It works four times faster and thanks you for your generosity
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q04.d=It explodes, as much as you'd like cable's rating does not increase the machine's rating
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q05.prompt=Two cables have the same voltage rating, but one supports more amps. What does the higher amp rating allow?
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q05.a=Sending a higher voltage safely into the same machine
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q05.b=Carrying more amperage without exceeding the cable's amp limit
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q05.c=Unlocking the cable's management career
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q05.d=Skipping MV because thick cables look like HV cables
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q06.prompt=You keep sending 4 A through a cable rated for 1 A. What should you expect?
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q06.a=The cable automatically upgrades itself
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q06.b=The extra amps wait in an orderly queue
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q06.c=The cable introduces you to Joule's law
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q06.d=The cable files a complaint but continues working
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q07.prompt=Ignoring cable losses, how much power is 2 A at 32 V?
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q07.a=64 EU/t
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q07.b=16 EU/t
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q07.c=128 EU/t
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q07.d=Two electricity. One for each amp
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q08.prompt=Why can a long, lossy cable make your machines struggle for power?
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q08.a=Electrons need a lunch break after every sixteen blocks
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q08.b=The cable charges rent per machine
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q08.c=Greg noticed you were enjoying yourself
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q08.d=Voltage drops faster than your motivation to finish this modpack
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q09.prompt=You have MV power and want to supply LV machines. What is the sensible solution?
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q09.a=Connect 4 LV machines in series and hope they share the voltage like good friends
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q09.b=Put a sign saying “32V ONLY” on the generator
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q09.c=You remember how long those machines took to craft and use a transformer
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q09.d=Connect it quickly before the machine notices
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q10.prompt=Can a normal LV machine use a cable rated for more amps than the machine needs?
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q10.a=No. The cable forces every available amp into the machine
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q10.b=Yes, though Greg is crying over your inefficient resource management
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q10.c=Only after the cable completes this exam too
gtnhextranerf.exam.lv.q10.d=Yes, but only if you apologize to Ohm
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.introduction=Welcome to the GregTech High Pressure Safety Board.\n\nYou are applying for permission to put extremely hot gas inside pipes and then live near those pipes. The Board considers this an unusual lifestyle choice but respects your commitment.\n\nOur previous operator left the facility in all directions. We are therefore introducing a written exam.\n\nAnswer at least 8 of the following 10 questions correctly. “It worked in another modpack” is not a recognized qualification.
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.passed=Congratulations! You are now a Certified High Pressure Operator.\n\nAfter all that mining, crafting, and paperwork, you are finally qualified to make water angry enough to flatten an ingot. Your family must be very proud.\n\nPlease avoid testing steam exhausts and hot pipes with your face. The Board considers your health bar an ongoing part of this assessment.
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.failed=Certification denied.\n\nBased on your answers, the Board expects your first practical demonstration to also be your last. Please study the material before trying again.
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q01.prompt=Before firing up a Small Coal Boiler, what should you provide?
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q01.a=Coal and a written apology to the nearest village
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q01.b=Water and suitable fuel, because even Greg hasn't found a way to boil nothing
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q01.c=Fuel only, water can be added once things get exciting
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q01.d=A steam tank, so the boiler knows what you expect from it
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q02.prompt=A Small Coal Boiler has run dry while above 100°C. What can happen if you add water while it is still hot?
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q02.a=It produces premium steam with extra confidence
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q02.b=The water cools it safely because water always fixes fire
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q02.c=It restarts normally after judging your bucket technique
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q02.d=It can explode and distribute your bronze investment across the neighborhood
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q03.prompt=How should you deal with that hot, dry Small Coal Boiler before refilling it?
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q03.a=Stop heating it and wait for 100°C or below before refilling, however urgently you want to get back to making plates
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q03.b=Add water quickly before the boiler notices
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q03.c=Add another stack of coal to boil away the problem
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q03.d=Stand farther away and ask a friend to refill it
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q04.prompt=What should you check when choosing a pipe for hot gas?
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q04.a=Whether its color matches the boiler
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q04.b=Whether the crafting recipe looked expensive enough
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q04.c=Gas tightness, temperature limit, and flow capacity, since Greg insists that looking like a pipe isn't enough
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q04.d=Whether it has already survived one explosion
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q05.prompt=What can happen when a pipe that is not gas-proof carries hot steam?
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q05.a=The steam stays inside because it respects private property
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q05.b=It can leak hot steam and turn your plumbing into a PvP build
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q05.c=It automatically seals itself after receiving enough complaints
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q05.d=It converts the steam into harmless clouds for decoration
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q06.prompt=A steam machine finished one recipe, but its exhaust is blocked by a solid block. What should you do?
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q06.a=Remove the block you placed there for aesthetic reasons and let the machine vent
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q06.b=Add more steam until the machine negotiates with the wall
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q06.c=Replace the block with a more expensive solid block
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q06.d=Report the wall for obstructing industrial progress
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q07.prompt=Where should you stand when a steam machine vents?
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q07.a=Directly in front of the exhaust, you paid for the whole machine including the sauna
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q07.b=In the exhaust block, holding a bucket to catch the steam
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q07.c=As close as possible, the particles are merely a weather forecast
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q07.d=Away from the exhaust unless you're volunteering to become the next steamed recipe
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q08.prompt=A Small Coal Boiler produces more steam than its internal tank can hold. What does it do?
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q08.a=Saves the extra steam in your inventory
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q08.b=Unlocks High Pressure II and doubles the blast radius
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q08.c=It vents the excess giving your hard-earned fuel a career in sound effects
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q08.d=Compresses the steam into a bronze ingot
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q09.prompt=During a full moon, on the third Tuesday after an inspection that never took place, a north-facing boiler at Y=73, installed exactly seven blocks west of a crafting table that has only ever been used to make other crafting tables, produces steam at a steady rate of 120 L per second. Its operator is carrying 17 cobblestone, has jumped three times for calibration, and is being supervised by a chicken whose engineering qualifications are currently under investigation. Given that the server maintains exactly 20 ticks per second, the water supply is uninterrupted, the safety board has not submitted a written objection, and the operator's friend insists that his cousin gets twice as much steam using the same setup but refuses to provide screenshots, what is the boiler's average steam output per tick, assuming Greg has approved the use of division for this calculation? Assume no TPS loss.
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q09.a=6 L/t
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q09.b=120 L/t
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q09.c=2,400 L/t
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q09.d=One bucket per emotional support session
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q10.prompt=Your machines consume more steam than your boilers produce. What solves the ongoing shortage?
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q10.a=Add a bigger tank since stored steam is legally required to last forever
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q10.b=Produce more steam or run fewer machines, however unfair you find the concept of supply and demand
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q10.c=Use wider pipes to persuade the boiler to produce more
gtnhextranerf.exam.steam.q10.d=Ignore the problem, maybe it'll fix itself

